meshes and curves with specified naming prefixes and parentage. Careful consideration is required regarding collection visibility when hiding linked collections, addressing previous findings.\n\n\nVerified a solution to cleanly link and hide the `V5_CarLightRec\n<truncated 7018 bytes>\n display size must remain compact or be hidden via their collection. This avoids unexpected behavior due to invalid display types. The script will explicitly save the `.blend` file after execution when a file path is provided, unless a `--no-save` flag is used, because the integration tests require that a subsequent run leaves the scene in the \"normal\" mode. The `v5_stills.py` script requires updating to render specified stills and generate a contact sheet, as per the current brief.\n\n\nThe `v5_stills.py` script will support two modes. In standalone Python mode, it copies frames from a specified directory to generate the contact sheet. Blender's render mode imports `bpy`, sets render parameters, and handles camera switching based on timeline markers. Crucially, the render script will explicitly ensure the scene camera matches the active marker camera before rendering each still and restore the scene camera afterward to ensure proper rendering in headless environments.\n\n\nVerifying that all still frames are rendered from the active shot camera at the specified frame numbers. Confirming that all frames in `SHOTS` within `v5_stills.py` showcase peak action: apexes, brake glows, and steering inputs. Comparing `SHOTS` against shot windows from `inspect_shots_and_cockpit.py` to ensure action frames fall cleanly within each shot's timeline. Specific action frames are under inspection.\n\n\nInspecting the specified frames confirms key action moments across each shot, validating the focus on peak action. Frame numbers are checked against defined time windows in the shot list for apexes, braking, and steering. This establishes the animation frames are correctly capturing intended action.\n