{"step_index":82,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:41:34Z","input_tokens":3347,"cache_read_tokens":193306,"output_tokens":20830,"thinking":"HUD dimensions are now understood as 67 cm^2, which is a holographic frame. Proceeding to carefully craft the `pipeline/v5_anim.py` script, ensuring adherence to the physics requirements.\n\n\nThe script's core rules define interpolation, heading, racing coordinates, and linear keyframes. Lateral acceleration constraints and specific object properties are also defined. Outliner hygiene requires moving the race rig to a collection and linking car light receivers and car lights into a lighting collection for organizational and visibility control.\n\n\nCreated `V5_08_Cameras` collection and linked all camera objects for organization. Verified the scene collection structure. Developed a brake disc and caliper thermal glow effect using a physical thermal state model to simulate rapid heating during braking and realistic cooling, with speed-weighted heat-up and convective cooling, visible in key cornering scenarios.\n\n\nDeveloped a brake disc thermal glow effect that varies between transparent and fiery red-orange based on brake heat. If pre-existing material customizations are found, they are preserved but updated to control emission based on brake heat. Emission drivers are added to existing principled BSDFs if they are missing, for rotor glow and caliper heat-soak.\n\n\nDedicated a single-user material `Mat_FIA_RainLight` with an emission color of (1.0, 0.02, 0.01). Implemented a rapid 6.0 Hz FIA strobe effect (strength of 24.0 / 1.2) for heavy braking and high-speed lift-off scenarios, with a dimmer tail glow (strength of 2.5) otherwise.\n\nAdjusted the steering wheel rotation ratio to 9.5 for authentic F1 steering wheel angles (±142° max) across the race rig and associated cockpit objects. Created dedicated shift-LED materials driven by the 8-speed within-gear RPM fraction and upshift flash for the shift LEDs on the steering wheel.\n\nA `V5_CamFocus` empty object was created in `V5_08_Cameras` to define the animated depth of field.\n\n\nCamera positions are precisely keyframed at 0.45m above the world position of the root bone. Depth of field is enabled and focused on the `V5_CamFocus` object for non-onboard cameras. Specific F-stop values are adjusted for each camera to achieve realistic broadcast depth of field, with calculated parameters for camera positioning to clear any potential obstructions.\n\n\nAdded camera positions and parameters for specific viewpoints: `Cam_S17_Maggotts` and `Bridge_B_Deck`. Defined onboard camera positions, including `Cam_S02_Onboard` (Halo/Over-Shoulder Gyro view) and `Cam_S19_Onboard3` (Cockpit Center Rollbar/Helmet view), ensuring proper tracking and visibility of key elements. Onboard cameras' `fwd` values were correctly retained.\n\nImplemented horizon roll coupling and deterministic micro-vibration for realistic camera dynamics.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nV5 ANIM — 真实赛道整圈（Silverstone / 90.34 s / 162 拍 / 2161 帧）\\n输入: LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend\\n输出: LATEST/v5_stage_anim.blend\\n运行:\\n  blender -b -P pipeline/v5_anim.py\\n  blender -b -P pipeline/v5_anim.py -- --test 60,160,350,760,1120,1640,1730\\n  blender -b -P pipeline/v5_anim.py -- --render\\n\\n五条硬规则（来自 track_data/TRACK_SPEC.md）\\n  1. 位置按 t 插值，不按帧均分\\n  2. 朝向取 heading_deg，不用位移差反推\\n  3. 位置走 racing_xy，不是 xy\\n  4. 关键帧 LINEAR，禁 Bezier\\n  5. v^2 * curv 不得超过 15.0 + 0.00714 v^2\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport bpy, json, math, os, sys, random\\nfrom mathutils import Vector, Matrix, Euler\\nfrom math import sin, cos, pi, radians, degrees, sqrt, exp\\n\\nPROJ = r\\\"D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\"\\nTRACK = os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"track_data\\\", \\\"silverstone_track.json\\\")\\nFRAMES_DIR = os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"renders_v5\\\", \\\"frames\\\")\\nSTILLS_DIR = os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"renders_v5\\\", \\\"stills\\\")\\n\\nARGV = sys.argv[sys.argv.index(\\\"--\\\") + 1:] if \\\"--\\\" in sys.argv else []\\n\\n\\ndef argval(flag, default=None):\\n    if flag in ARGV:\\n        i = ARGV.index(flag)\\n        if i + 1 < len(ARGV) and not ARGV[i + 1].startswith(\\\"--\\\"):\\n            return ARGV[i + 1]\\n        return True\\n    return default\\n\\n\\nIN = argval(\\\"--in\\\", os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"LATEST\\\", \\\"v5_stage_env.blend\\\"))\\nOUT = argval(\\\"--out\\\", os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"LATEST\\\", \\\"v5_stage_anim.blend\\\"))\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 0. 参数\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------\\nFPS = 24\\nBEAT = 60.0 / 108.0                 # After Hours 108 BPM -> 0.5556 s\\nBEAT_F = BEAT * FPS                 # 13.3333 帧\\nTOTAL_BEATS = 162\\nFRAME_END = int(round(1 + TOTAL_BEATS * BEAT_F))    # 2161\\nR_TIRE = 0.357\\nWHEELBASE = 3.6\\n\\ndata = json.load(open(TRACK, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\nMETA = data[\\\"meta\\\"]\\nP = data[\\\"points\\\"]\\nN = len(P)\\nLAP_S = META[\\\"sim_lap_s\\\"]           # \n<truncated 44533 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"d:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\\pipeline\\\\v5_anim.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
